        "【Litigation】15 July 2016: sued the FDA over the deeming rule together with the CAA and CRA (federal district court, District of Columbia)",
        "【Litigation】The warning-label requirement held arbitrary and capricious on appeal, and subsequently vacated",
        "【Litigation】5 July 2022: summary judgment for the plaintiffs on the FDA's failure to exempt premium cigars",
        "【Litigation】August 2023: the deeming rule vacated as it applies to premium cigars",
        "【Litigation】January 2026: the appeals court finds for the industry three to nil (the definition remanded); 16 April of that year, the district court reaffirms the vacatur",
        "【Organisation】Headquartered in Washington, D.C. Scott Pearce, in post from 2018, stepped down in 2024, succeeded by Joshua Habursky",
