      trivia: "【A Body That Has Changed Its Name Three Times】The RTDA of 1933, the IPCPR of 2007, the PCA of 2019. With each renaming the remit shifted — from tobacco retailing at large, to the specialist premium cigar and pipe shop, and on to the premium cigar industry as a whole — narrowing here, broadening there.\n【From July to Spring】The trade show, long a fixture of midsummer Las Vegas, moved to March in 2024 and to New Orleans from 2025. Since the change of dates and venue, the association reports, retail accounts have grown by about 14.8 per cent.\n【The FDA Suit as a Ten Years' War】From the filing of July 2016 to the district court's decision of April 2026, the fight ran a full decade. The judgment's effect is retroactive: premium cigars meeting the definition are treated as having been outside the regulation even for the period from 8 August 2016 to 9 August 2023."
